        "characterization_summary": "Lower aging temperature causes (003) and (006) peaks to broaden and weaken, indicating lower crystallinity; (003) reflection shifts from 8.04 Å (24:0) to 7.82 Å (24:2) to 7.69 Å (24:4) at RT.",
        "evidence_snippet": "The corresponding XRD spectra (Fig. 1e and S2a and b†) showed that the (003) and the (006) peaks were significantly broadened and weaken with depressed aging temperature... with the more NO3^- exchanged by CO3^2- in the synthesis step 24:0 to 24:4), the (003) Bragg reflection gradually shifted from 8.04 Å to 7.82 Å and then to 7.69 Å.",
        "related_images": [
          "6f2a5f734b3960527fb87adaad9859e652282e425689a38c2989bcc2a6ef7074.jpg"
        ],
